Subject: Register VM: the activation counter table reports its length

What this does
  - quickjs.c: qjs_aot_icount_table() returns the number of counters (the unit table's size) through its argument.

Why we need it
  The unit's report read QJS_AOT_NFUNCS counters from a table allocated for the unit table's count; the functions past it printed heap garbage.

Soundness
  Read-only.

Failure modes
  None.

--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -68604,8 +68604,9 @@
 uint64_t *js_aot_icount;
 
 /* The unit's report reads the counters through this (a weak reference there, so a unit also links against an engine without it). */
-const uint64_t *qjs_aot_icount_table(void)
+const uint64_t *qjs_aot_icount_table(unsigned *n)
 {
+    *n = js_aot_icount != NULL ? (unsigned)qjs_aot_count : 0u;
     return js_aot_icount;
 }
 #endif
